{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37213790",
      "title": "Adding Validation Logic",
      "lectureOrder": 216,
      "videoOrder": 200,
      "sourceHash": "3c3844f4367aa8bfa0687efc9d96bc52d31c0fb0b46d18324df5f993926c7d58",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 2.903,
          "en": "So let's start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.903,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "with validating user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 6.48,
          "en": "For that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.48,
          "end": 9.6,
          "en": "we already got this validator function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 12.15,
          "en": "It's not doing anything meaningful right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.15,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "but I mentioned earlier that this is a special parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "that can be set on that text form field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 21.12,
          "en": "which in the end wants a function that will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.12,
          "end": 25.92,
          "en": "by Flutter by this form in the end, as you will soon see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 27.96,
          "en": "to run some validation logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.96,
          "end": 32.19,
          "en": "and return an error message if validation fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.19,
          "end": 35.043,
          "en": "Otherwise, this function should return null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.12,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "So if it does return null, Flutter knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 42.66,
          "en": "that validation succeeded and the entered value is correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.66,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "Otherwise, if we return some text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "this will be the error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 48.93,
          "en": "and this will tell Flutter that validation failed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.93,
          "end": 51.51,
          "en": "and the entered value is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.51,
          "end": 55.08,
          "en": "So therefore, here in this validator function, we can work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.08,
          "end": 57.09,
          "en": "with that value which will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.09,
          "end": 60.99,
          "en": "provided by Flutter when this function here is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.99,
          "end": 63.6,
          "en": "And this value here will be the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.6,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "that's currently entered into this field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "and we can then use a if check to check whether it's valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 72.123,
          "en": "For example, we can check if it's null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.26,
          "end": 75.6,
          "en": "This is not the only check I want to perform though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.6,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "Instead I will add another check here combined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "with the first check through the logical or operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 85.86,
          "en": "so that even if this here is not true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.86,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "So if the value is not null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 90.6,
          "en": "we still perform the second condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 94.17,
          "en": "And my second condition here is whether value is empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.17,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "so not null, but an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 99.50999999999999,
          "en": "With that, we would make it into this if block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.50999999999999,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "if either the value is null or if value is empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 107.52000000000001,
          "en": "It's also worth knowing that if value is null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.52000000000001,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "this second check won't even be performed by Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "because it already has one true value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 115.38,
          "en": "if value is null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.38,
          "end": 116.67,
          "en": "and that is all it needs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.67,
          "end": 118.62,
          "en": "If at least one of the conditions is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.62,
          "end": 120.09,
          "en": "we make it into the if block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.09,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "So in that case, the other conditions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 123.693,
          "en": "wouldn't even be evaluated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 127.29,
          "en": "Of course, that's different when using the and operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.29,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "Here, all conditions must be met",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 131.76,
          "en": "and therefore all conditions will be evaluated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 131.76,
          "end": 134.55,
          "en": "With or, one matching condition is enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.55,
          "end": 138.183,
          "en": "to skip the other conditions and make it into this if block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.29,
          "end": 141.54,
          "en": "But even with those two conditions here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.54,
          "end": 143.76,
          "en": "I don't have all the checks I wanna have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.76,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "I'll add another or operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 148.71,
          "en": "to add another condition, another check here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.71,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "And you can add and combine as many conditions as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 155.79,
          "en": "You can also combine or and and if you needed to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 157.2,
          "en": "but here I'll stick to or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "because I have a lot of alternative checks which I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 162.21,
          "en": "to perform, and if one of them is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 162.21,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "I wanna make it into this if block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 168.81,
          "en": "because my next check here is whether a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 168.81,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "once trimmed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "And you might recall that trim is a built-in method which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "you can execute on strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 179.19,
          "en": "to remove excess white space at the beginning and end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 179.19,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "So once the value is trimmed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "and we got rid of any excess white space,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 186.24,
          "en": "I wanna check if the length is equal to one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 186.24,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "Because here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 191.55,
          "en": "I want to have input values, names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 191.55,
          "end": 194.34,
          "en": "that are at least two characters long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 194.34,
          "end": 197.673,
          "en": "So if the length is one, I'm not happy with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 198.69,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "And actually we can check for smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 203.97,
          "en": "or equal than one to make sure that if the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 203.97,
          "end": 206.57999999999998,
          "en": "after trimming it would have a length of zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 206.57999999999998,
          "end": 208.803,
          "en": "We also make it into this if block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 210.36,
          "end": 213.09,
          "en": "And now there's one last condition I want to add here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 213.09,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "and that is that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 220.1,
          "en": "after trimmed has a length greater than 50",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.68,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "because I want to have a max length of 50,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 226.5,
          "en": "which is also why I set this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 229.14,
          "en": "And indeed setting this parameter should ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 229.14,
          "end": 231.84,
          "en": "that you can't enter more than 50 characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 231.84,
          "end": 235.023,
          "en": "But still it doesn't hurt to also add this check here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 236.22,
          "end": 238.07999999999998,
          "en": "And now I add the curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 240.27,
          "en": "to define my if statement body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 240.27,
          "end": 243.66,
          "en": "and will now only make it into this body here if at least",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 243.66,
          "end": 245.21,
          "en": "one of these conditions is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 246.81,
          "end": 248.46,
          "en": "Now, it's then in this body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 248.46,
          "end": 250.86,
          "en": "where I wanna return my error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.86,
          "end": 253.74,
          "en": "And of course here I want to say something more meaningful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 253.74,
          "end": 257.13,
          "en": "Like for example, must be between one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 257.13,
          "end": 261.633,
          "en": "and 50 characters long or just characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 263.1,
          "end": 267.66,
          "en": "And otherwise after this if statement, I wanna return null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.66,
          "end": 270.63,
          "en": "So this will execute if we don't make it into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.63,
          "end": 273.24,
          "en": "this if statement, because then we do indeed have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.24,
          "end": 274.71,
          "en": "a valid input value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 274.71,
          "end": 277.40999999999997,
          "en": "And then I wanna return null to tell Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 277.40999999999997,
          "end": 279.003,
          "en": "that value is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 280.17,
          "end": 282.87,
          "en": "If we make it into this if block here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 282.87,
          "end": 285.81,
          "en": "we'll instead return this, this error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 285.81,
          "end": 288.543,
          "en": "and that will tell Flutter that something went wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 289.65,
          "end": 291.39,
          "en": "Now with that, if you save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 291.39,
          "end": 293.61,
          "en": "and force a reload, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 293.61,
          "end": 295.8,
          "en": "that this has no effect though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 295.8,
          "end": 299.64,
          "en": "If I enter something here and I delete it and this is empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 299.64,
          "end": 302.01,
          "en": "and I for example, click add item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 302.01,
          "end": 304.47,
          "en": "I don't see this error message anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 304.47,
          "end": 308.46,
          "en": "Instead we'll have to trigger this validation function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 308.46,
          "end": 312.12,
          "en": "We'll have to tell Flutter to trigger it to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 312.12,
          "end": 314.49,
          "en": "and we'll do so in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 314.49,
          "end": 316.56,
          "en": "But before we go there, I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 316.56,
          "end": 319.12,
          "en": "to copy this validator parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 320.13,
          "end": 323.16,
          "en": "and also add that to my other text form field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 323.16,
          "end": 326.1,
          "en": "which is about entering a quantity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 326.1,
          "end": 328.26,
          "en": "There I will add it as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 328.26,
          "end": 330.99,
          "en": "but here the checks will be different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 330.99,
          "end": 333.6,
          "en": "Here I wanna make sure that it's not null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 333.6,
          "end": 336.96,
          "en": "or if it is null, I wanna make it into this if statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 336.96,
          "end": 338.85,
          "en": "and return an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 338.85,
          "end": 340.95,
          "en": "And I want to check whether it's empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 340.95,
          "end": 343.74,
          "en": "but thereafter I'm not interested in the length.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 343.74,
          "end": 345.21,
          "en": "But instead here in the end, I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 345.21,
          "end": 346.62,
          "en": "to get a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 346.62,
          "end": 349.35,
          "en": "As a string, as you learned, it's always a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 349.35,
          "end": 351.21,
          "en": "but I want to treat it as a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 351.21,
          "end": 353.55,
          "en": "and handle it as a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 353.55,
          "end": 356.82,
          "en": "And to do that I'll add int.tryParse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 356.82,
          "end": 360.39,
          "en": "so that I try converting the entered value to a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 360.39,
          "end": 361.8,
          "en": "And if this is null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 361.8,
          "end": 364.26,
          "en": "I also wanna make it into this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 364.26,
          "end": 366.99,
          "en": "because tryParse returns null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 366.99,
          "end": 370.59,
          "en": "if it fails to convert the string to a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 370.59,
          "end": 372.84,
          "en": "As you can, for example, see it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
